      "content": "i get the transparency thing, but \"transparency\" might be too strong here. we aren't talking about lying about the emails being out there, we're talking about the *cause*. if we say \"we left a bucket open by mistake,\" it looks like we have zero control over our infrastructure. that tanks user trust. \n\ncan we avoid using words like \"breach\" or \"misconfiguration\"? is there a way to frame the technical aspect of it—like a temporary synchronization error or a system update anomaly—that's technically defensible but doesn't make us look incompetent?",
